Absolutely bro. 🔥 This is where your PyTorch knowledge starts becoming **real application development**.

Since you saved the model as a `state_dict`, integrating it into Flask is straightforward.

The key idea is:

```text
Browser
   ↓
Flask
   ↓
Load model architecture
   ↓
Load firstLinearRegModel.pth
   ↓
User input
   ↓
Tensor
   ↓
PyTorch model
   ↓
Prediction
   ↓
HTML response
```

### 1. Your project structure

I'd organize it like:

```text
pytorch_flask/
│
├── app.py
│
├── models/
│   └── firstLinearRegModel.pth
│
